% ============================================================================
% mitosis-phase-ordinal-position.query.adj — worked recall over the
% mitosis-phase/ordinal bridge library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what position is this
% phase of mitosis, in words?" — it states no fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded rule and asks binding queries. The answer is
% DERIVED, joining a phase-order fact to an ordinal-word fact, so every
% answer carries BOTH citations in its `steps` trail.
%
% Placed at the stdlib PACKAGE ROOT (not beside `biology/mitosis-phase-
% ordinal-position.adj`) — the same cross-directory-import sandboxing
% pattern `astronomy/planet-ordinal-position.query.adj` (and, before it,
% `season-start-month-number.query.adj`) already established: the library
% itself lives in `biology/` and reaches its mathematics sibling via a
% relative `../mathematics/ordinal-numbers.adj` import, which only resolves
% if the CONSUMING entry program (this file) sits at or above the package
% root.
%
% Run (from this directory, the package root, so the relative import
% resolves):
%     ../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli mitosis-phase-ordinal-position.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "biology/mitosis-phase-ordinal-position.adj"

? mitosis_phase_ordinal_position(anaphase, $O)      % expect third  (direct: what position is anaphase, in words?)
? mitosis_phase_ordinal_position($P, first)         % expect prophase (reverse: which phase is first?)
? mitosis_phase_ordinal_position(interphase, $O)    % expect abstain -- interphase is not one of the 4 ordered mitotic phases
